    "body": "This proposes `_` as an unspendable Taproot internal-key placeholder in wallet policies. Wallets and signers can reproduce the internal key from the policy and derivation path, without keeping a separate random tweak.\n\nThe construction uses the BIP 341 NUMS point as the public key of a synthetic BIP 32 root. Its chain code commits to the normalized policy, including both the keys and the policy structure. Child keys are then derived using unhardened BIP 32 derivation.\n\nThis builds on the [Delving discussion](https://delvingbitcoin.org/t/unspendable-keys-in-descriptors/304) and the earlier work in #1746. I shared an earlier draft on the [Bitcoin Development Mailing List](https://groups.google.com/g/bitcoindev/c/se3TkNnbno4).\n\nI've included a Python reference implementation, fixed JSON test vectors, and instructions for running the checks. All 21 offline tests pass, and the export and derivation cross-check passes all 20 cases against Bitcoin Core 31.0.",
